// ───────────────────────────── build 32.2 · presses never bounce, the contact form, the wait-list form, one row per submission ─────────────────────────────

/**
 * A press that cannot get the script lock is kept and written by the next holder of the lock, and the caller is told ok.
 * run() holds the lock for a minute or two every five; a press used to wait fifteen seconds and then answer busy, and the page rolled the card back.
 * Now: pressLock_ waits PRESS_WAIT_MS_, and when the lock is still not free it keeps the press (pressKeep_) and answers { ok: true, queued: true }.
 * The kept presses are written in the order pressed (pressFlush_) at the start of run(), at the end of run() just before the feed is written, and by the next
 * press that gets the lock, so a press never waits more than one run. Kept in Script Properties (pq:<time>-<id>:<part>), not the cache: the cache cannot list its
 * keys and may drop an entry early, and a press that is dropped is worse than one that bounced. A property holds 9 KB, so a press is cut into parts of 2,400 characters.
 * The desk key is never kept: the press is kept with the person it was pressed by (who) and replayed as that person.
 */
