// ───────────────────────────── build 33 · every press tells the truth ─────────────────────────────
// John Sherrod, Nov 7, 2026: "every press tells the truth." A card closes because the record proves it, because a person said it was done, or because the press changed another
// record, and the Actions tab says which. The values of the "closed how" column:
//   Proven               the record shows it (a session on the calendar, his agreement on file, our ask in sent mail, the live page carrying the new words)
//   Said done            a person pressed Done (or Handled another way); nothing was proven
//   Changed <record>     the press changed another record: Changed The Moves, Changed the Sources list, Changed What’s New
//   Dropped              a person pressed Drop, or a card untouched for 37 days dropped itself (30 days, then seven to answer Drop or keep)
//   Lapsed               the thing that asked for the card changed (a new week, a new recommendation) and nothing was shown to be done
